{title: When the Saints Go Marching In}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: C}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Oh when the [C]saints go marching [G7]in
Oh when the [C]saints go marching in
Oh [C7]Lord, I want to [F]be in that [C]number
When the [G7]saints go marching [C]in
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
And when the [C]sun refuse to [G7]shine
And when the [C]sun refuse to shine
Oh [C7]Lord, I want to [F]be in that [C]number
When the [G7]sun refuse to [C]shine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Oh when the [C]trumpet sounds its [G7]call
Oh when the [C]trumpet sounds its call
Oh [C7]Lord, I want to [F]be in that [C]number
When the [G7]trumpet sounds its [C]call
{end_of_verse}
